{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9yW8gKfuQnYfcV4Vi5c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: patterns given with `--and` now get the same path-separator error as the main pattern. Before, only the main pattern was checked, so something like `fd foo --and one/two` quietly found nothing instead of explaining why.\n\n- **Change (`src/main.rs`):** `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now runs the check on the main pattern and on every `--and` pattern. I moved the check itself into a new helper, `ensure_pattern_has_no_path_separator`, without changing what it does. `--full-path` still turns the check off for all patterns.\n- **Test:** I added `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected` in `tests/tests.rs`. The gate result was **GATE PASS**: the test fails with the old code and passes with the fix, and the format and leftover-debug checks were clean.\n- **Not checked:** I didn't run the full test suite. I also didn't test the Windows-only `\\` case for `--and` patterns, because this machine is Linux and that code is only compiled on Windows."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":35902,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":792,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc1329c8-50c1-4e60-a470-3ed5381008c9","uuid":"14263886-4474-4a84-9022-56a5a7140576","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:55:40.655Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9yW8UfKubWmHuUEiAtq"}
